A set of mutually exclusive options - pick exactly one.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/radio)

<%= embed AppicaUI::RadioPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
RadioGroup(name: "plan", default_value: "pro", aria_label: "Plan") do
  label(class: "flex items-center gap-2") { Radio(value: "free"); plain "Free" }
  label(class: "flex items-center gap-2") { Radio(value: "pro"); plain "Pro" }
end
```

Each `Radio` is a native `<input type="radio">` sharing the group's `name:`, so the browser handles the selection,
the arrow keys (one tab stop per group) and form submission. The group picks the checked option from
`default_value:` and passes `disabled:` / `required:` to every option. Radios are sized in `em`.

